=== sentence windows findings lean on (seconds, factors 0.8 / 1.0 / 1.25)
  02_1 s0:  4.62 /  5.77 /  7.21  'Our drawing rule asks for a function whose derivative equals itself, starting at one.'
  02_1 s1:  0.92 /  1.15 /  1.44  'Try a polynomial.'
  02_3 s3:  1.80 /  2.24 /  2.81  'Those denominators are factorials.'
  02_5 s1:  4.53 /  5.66 /  7.08  'The ratio of one absolute term to the previous one is at most R divided by its index.'
  02_5 s2:  2.24 /  2.80 /  3.50  'Eventually that ratio is at most one half.'
  02_5 s4:  2.67 /  3.33 /  4.16  'The same argument works for the derivative series.'
  03_2 s0:  4.17 /  5.21 /  6.51  'Instead of collecting the products by rows, collect them by total degree.'
  03_5 s2:  3.00 /  3.75 /  4.69  'The diagonals are precisely the terms of E at x plus y.'
  01_5 s0:  4.16 /  5.20 /  6.50  'A curve whose slope equals its height would solve our drawing rule exactly.'
  01_5 s1:  6.88 /  8.60 / 10.75  'We have not yet proved that the stepped approximations reach such a curve, or that only one such curve starts at height one.'
